 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "694c37ef6ab3a41370d83ffa",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "level": 1,
     "text": "Apartment interior design in Eurovea City, Bratislava, custom furniture, 56 m²"
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "parts": [
      {
       "t": "p",
       "html": "An interior design project for a 56 m² apartment in Eurovea City in Bratislava under the <a href=\"/en/custom-furniture-bratislava-design-production\">“Furniture” design package</a>. We worked with the developer’s finishes: we developed the interior concept, produced 3D visualizations and technical documentation, designed the cabinet furniture and had it custom-made in Bratislava. Upholstered furniture, lighting and decor were selected separately, and materials were chosen with the budget in mind. The project included design supervision."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "level": 2,
     "text": "Layout"
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "parts": [
      {
       "t": "p",
       "html": "According to the measured floor plan, the apartment has a 28.2 m² kitchen-living room, a 16.1 m² bedroom, a 5.7 m² entrance hall, a 4.4 m² bathroom and a 1.6 m² utility space used as a laundry room. The kitchen-living room and the bedroom have floor-to-ceiling windows, and the apartment has a terrace."
      },
      {
       "t": "p",
       "html": "The kitchen-living room is the main space. The kitchen runs along the wall, with an island in front of it topped by a thick light stone-look countertop. By the window is a round dark wood dining table with wood-framed chairs and a pendant of two fluted discs above it. Opposite the kitchen are a light sofa and a dark wood chest of drawers, and the TV area has a dark gray wall with a low wooden media unit."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "level": 2,
     "text": "Custom furniture"
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "parts": [
      {
       "t": "p",
       "html": "The cabinet furniture was designed together with the interior, so the cabinets are built into the niches and the corridor. The kitchen has tall units with wood fronts, one of which houses two ovens. The upper cabinets are light gray and handleless, with lighting underneath. The corridor from the entrance to the kitchen is lined with floor-to-ceiling cabinets: some fronts are fluted and some are mirrored, which makes the passage look wider."
      },
      {
       "t": "p",
       "html": "In the bedroom, a floor-to-ceiling wardrobe runs along one wall, the wall behind the bed is finished in wood panels, and the headboard is gray and upholstered. By the window is a workspace with a narrow desk and a wall-hung drawer unit, and the lower part of the wall is clad in wood."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "level": 2,
     "text": "Color and light"
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "parts": [
      {
       "t": "p",
       "html": "The palette is calm: white walls, wood in two tones, light stone, dark gray doors and the TV wall. The floor throughout the apartment is oak-look. Above the kitchen there is a black track with spotlights, the living room has linear sconces, and the entrance hall has a ceiling light made of light rings."
      }
     ]
    },
